### 🔗 2. Internal Linking Rules & Anchor Text Map

To avoid over-optimization penalties, anchor text must be diverse (exact match, partial match, and natural language). 

#### **Rule A: Pillar to Spokes (Top-Down)**
The main pillar page (`nuevas-camaras-2026.html`) must contain **at least one contextual link** to every spoke page in its body, plus a dedicated "Related Guides" grid at the bottom.

| Target Spoke | Recommended Anchor Text (Natural Spanish) | Placement |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Spoke 1 (Travel) | "mejor cámara para viajar en 2026" | Body paragraph discussing travel scenarios |
| Spoke 2 (Budget) | "mejores opciones de cámaras baratas por menos de 500€" | Body paragraph discussing budget constraints |
| Spoke 3 (Vlogging) | "guía de las mejores cámaras para vlogging" | Body paragraph discussing content creation |
| Spoke 4 (Action) | "cámaras deportivas y acuáticas resistentes" | Body paragraph discussing beach/outdoor use |
| Spoke 5 (Calendar) | "Calendario de Lanzamientos de Cámaras 2026" | Callout box about upcoming releases |
| Spoke 6 (Review) | "análisis completo de la Fujifilm X100VI en España" | Body paragraph mentioning the X100VI |

#### **Rule B: Spokes to Pillar (Bottom-Up)**
**Every single spoke page** must link back to the pillar page within the **first 100 words** of the introduction.
*   *Example Anchor:* "Como parte de nuestra [guía definitiva de nuevas cámaras en 2026](/es-es/guias/nuevas-camaras-2026.html), hemos evaluado..."

#### **Rule C: Spoke to Spoke (Lateral Linking)**
Cross-link related spokes to keep users in the silo. 
*   *Travel Page* → links to *Action Page* with anchor: "si planeas ir a la playa, consulta nuestras [cámaras acuáticas recomendadas](...)".
*   *Budget Page* → links to *Vlogging Page* with anchor: "para empezar en YouTube sin gastar mucho, mira las [mejores cámaras para vlogging económicas](...)".

